+<p>Every UM vendor stores our member ID in its own shape. A THP Medicare (TMP) or SCO card prints 9 characters; our systems store those 9 characters, three spaces and the suffix <code>01</code> (14 characters); eviCore, Evolent and Carelon keep 11 characters without the spaces, MHK keeps all 14, Optum keeps only the 9 characters printed on the card. EMRs type whatever is on the card. Today the mismatch surfaces at the vendor. This service moves the check to the front of the flow: one call from Onyx, one call to MMI, and back come the ID as received, the ID it resolved to, that ID in every vendor's format with the payer for that vendor's request, the coverage flag and an id for the coverage period. One operation, <code>POST /v1/interop/resolve</code>, gives every vendor's format at once, so one call serves a prior authorization whose codes go to several vendors. Once MMI has identified the member, a second internal call, to the member information service, fetches the member's coverage records; the one covering the date of service gives the line of business Onyx routes on (section 9.5).</p>
 
