 <ol>
 <li><b>Correlation.</b> Read <code>X-Correlation-Id</code> (or generate a UUID); it goes into every log line, the <code>X-Correlation-Id</code> response header and the body of error responses.</li>
 <li><b>Read the JSON.</b> Malformed JSON or a wrong JSON type is a 400. An unknown property, a <code>vendor</code> included, is ignored: the request type is declared <code>@JsonIgnoreProperties(ignoreUnknown = true)</code>.</li>
 <li><b>Validate in one pass.</b> Caller identification (<code>clientId</code>, <code>clientType</code> <code>EXT</code> or <code>INT</code>, <code>requestId</code>; a usable <code>requestId</code> joins the log context at once and is echoed even when another field fails); member ID present (the only check on it); date of service (a real <code>yyyy-MM-dd</code> date, not more than 10 years back, no upper limit; default to today only when omitted), end of a period of service, date of birth (format, plausibility). A sent date is always the date judged, never replaced by today. Every problem is returned together as one 400. No MMI call for an invalid request.</li>
-<li><b>Call MMI once</b> with the member id exactly as received, surrounding whitespace removed (section 8), in both <code>memberId</code> and <code>legacyMemberId</code>, <code>voidCoverageRecord = N</code>, this service's <code>clientId</code>, a fresh MMI <code>requestId</code> (section 9).</li>
