 <li><b>Interpret the answer</b> (section 9.3). MMI's HTTP 404 means "no member for this id": 200 NOT_FOUND, and what MMI said goes into <code>sourceMessage</code>. A 200 with no members is NOT_FOUND too, unless it carries an error-typed message (for example <code>ES_TIMEOUT</code>), which is a 502 forwarding MMI's code and text. MMI's 400 has already become a 400 <code>MEMBER_LOOKUP_REJECTED</code> and its 500 a 503 <code>MEMBER_LOOKUP_UNAVAILABLE</code> in the client, both carrying MMI's code and text. Otherwise map each record, keeping only readable, non-void coverage spans. A member with unreadable spans and no readable one is a 502, never a confident INACTIVE.</li>
