 <p>MMI's contract has four answers: 200 success, 404 member not found, 400 bad request, 500 internal error. This service maps them one to one: on 200 the records decide the outcome; MMI's 404 is <span class="pill ok">200</span> <code>NOT_FOUND</code>; MMI's 400 is <span class="pill bad">400</span> <code>MEMBER_LOOKUP_REJECTED</code> with MMI's text; MMI's 500 is <span class="pill bad">503</span> <code>MEMBER_LOOKUP_UNAVAILABLE</code>. Only an unknown route of this service is a 404 from this service. The mapping is fixed in <code>RestMmiClient</code> and <code>ResolutionService</code>; nothing about it is configurable. MMI's first message is returned to Onyx as <code>sourceMessage</code> on NOT_FOUND, and MMI's message code and text are appended to the 400 and 503 messages when MMI sent them. Any status outside the four is not MMI speaking but a gateway, proxy or container, and the answer says so.</p>
