+<h3>9.5 The member information service (line of business)</h3>
+<p>Once MMI has identified the member (ACTIVE or INACTIVE; never for NOT_FOUND, AMBIGUOUS or a rejected request), the service asks the member information service for that member's coverage records. The line of business Onyx routes on is derived from the record that covers the date of service: MMI's own <code>lineOfBusiness</code> is not the routing value, and the answer's <code>memberPlan</code> is not read, because it is not the plan on the date of service.</p>
+<pre><code>POST {member-info.base-url}/members      (plain HTTP, no auth, like MMI)
+Content-Type: application/json · Accept: application/json · X-Correlation-Id: &lt;onyx id&gt;
+
+{ "memberIds": [ "&lt;the resolved id, as MMI stores it&gt;" ], "dos": "10/15/2026", "returnCoverageList": true }
+
+→ { "requestId": null,
+    "members": [ { "requestId": null, "memberId": "&lt;as requested&gt;",
+                   "memberPlan": { ... },                         not read
+                   "coverageRecords": [                           about the last five years
+                     { benefitId, businessLineKey, businessTypeIndicator, carrier, carrierCode, gridId, groupId, ratingState,
+                       homeGroupId, network, networkId, planCode, planStartDate, planEndDate, planName, planType, productCode,
+                       sourceSystemId, subsidiary, voidFlag, ipa, hierarchyLineOfBusiness, hierarchyCompany,
+                       hierarchyCompanyDesc, lineOfBusinessDesc }, ... ] } ] }</code></pre>
+<ul>
+<li>One id per call: the resolved id exactly as MMI stores it (for a TMP member the 9 characters, three spaces and the suffix); <code>dos</code>, the date of service (the first day of a period), as <code>MM/dd/yyyy</code>; and <code>returnCoverageList</code>, always <code>true</code>.</li>
+<li><b>The records read.</b> Those of the entries whose <code>memberId</code> matches the resolved id ignoring spacing and case, void records (<code>voidFlag</code> Y) left out, in the order sent. Of those, only the records whose <code>planStartDate</code> and <code>planEndDate</code> include the date of service, both ends inclusive. A plan date is read as the date written (<code>2024-02-01T05:00:00.000+00:00</code> is 2024-02-01); no end date is open-ended; a record without a start, or with a date that cannot be read, covers nothing.</li>
+<li><b>The line of business</b> is derived in <code>LineOfBusinessDeriver</code> from the member portal's "ES Members" criteria, read against a covering record: <code>sourceSysId</code> is the record's <code>sourceSystemId</code>, <code>coverage.subsidiary</code> its <code>subsidiary</code> and <code>coverage.product</code> its <code>productCode</code>. SCO is read from <code>businessTypeIndicator</code> SH and a <code>planCode</code> with SCO in it, and is checked first, so an SCO record is never read as another value. MA-HMO and MA-PPO (<code>businessTypeIndicator</code> SH, <code>subsidiary</code> TAHMO, <code>businessLineKey</code> compared as the four digits) come next. Codes are compared ignoring case and surrounding spaces; the ES Members rules do not overlap. When several records cover the date, the first one a rule matches gives the value, and <code>marker=LOB_SEVERAL_ON_DATE</code> is logged if they disagree. A derived value is logged as <code>lob derived</code> with the record's fields and dates; otherwise <code>marker=LOB_NOT_DERIVED</code> with the number of records and of covering ones, and the first covering record's fields (<code>sourceSystemId</code>, <code>subsidiary</code>, <code>productCode</code>, <code>planCode</code>, <code>businessTypeIndicator</code>, <code>hierarchyLineOfBusiness</code>, <code>lineOfBusinessDesc</code>), so a PQA run shows what each uncovered member's record carries. TMP members are covered by MA-HMO and MA-PPO; their IPA variant is pending (below).</li>
+</ul>
+<div class="tablewrap"><table class="tight">
+<thead><tr><th><code>lineOfBusiness</code></th><th>Coverage record covering the date of service (the member portal's "ES Members" criteria)</th></tr></thead>
+<tbody>
