+<p><b>Pending, with CRC:</b> MA-HMO and MA-PPO may need an IPA variant. The record's <code>ipa</code> is to be checked against the CRC RTU tables, where MA-HMO may become an MA-HMO IPA value and MA-PPO an MA-PPO IPA value; the values and the table access are to be confirmed with CRC. The place for that lookup is marked in <code>LineOfBusinessDeriver</code>.</p>
+<ul>
+<li><b>Answers.</b> 200 is parsed; unknown fields are ignored. 404 is taken as "no records" and logged with <code>marker=MEMBER_PLAN_404</code> (a wrong URL looks the same). Unreachable, a timeout, 5xx, 429 or 408 is 503 <code>MEMBER_PLAN_UNAVAILABLE</code> with <code>Retry-After: 10</code>; any other status is 502 <code>MEMBER_PLAN_ERROR</code>; an empty, unreadable or <code>null</code> body is 502 <code>MEMBER_PLAN_INVALID_RESPONSE</code>. Each carries MMI's request id as <code>traceId</code>. The answer fails rather than going out without the records, because the line of business decides where Onyx routes the transaction. The service's own error contract is not documented yet (section 19).</li>
