 <h2 id="project"><span class="num">16</span>Project layout, build, STS, Postman</h2>
 <p>Standalone Gradle project <code>interop-resolution-service/</code>, built exactly like the EPA Workbench and the member profile service: Gradle 9.5.0 wrapper, Spring Boot 4.0.7 (Spring Framework 7, Jackson 3), Groovy DSL, no toolchain block, <code>options.release = 17</code> plus <code>-parameters</code> (and <code>java.sourceCompatibility</code> / <code>targetCompatibility</code> 17, which STS reads for the Eclipse project's Java level), <code>springBoot { buildInfo() }</code>, an <code>internalRepoUrl</code> property that swaps Maven Central for an internal mirror, <code>run.sh</code> / <code>run.cmd</code> launchers. Builds on JDK 17, 21 or 25. Dependencies: <code>spring-boot-starter-webmvc</code>, <code>-restclient</code>, <code>-jackson</code>, <code>-validation</code>, <code>-actuator</code>, <code>springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui</code> 3.0.3; tests use <code>spring-boot-starter-test</code> and <code>-webmvc-test</code>; <code>spring-boot-configuration-processor</code> as an annotation processor generates the metadata that makes STS know <code>mmi.*</code> and <code>member-id.*</code>. No Lombok, no JPA, no Resilience4j, no WireMock.</p>
